<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex reports March average crude exports.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex reports March average crude exports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said on Monday it exported an average 1.679 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude in March.</p>
<p>This figure compares with 1.449 million bpd exported the same month a year ago.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of crudes by type and destination:</p>
<p>  Maya exports			   1,004,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To North America		     777,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To Europe				220,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To Far East				7,000 bpd</p>
<p>  Isthmus exports			  174,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To North America		     104,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To Europe				 22,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To Far East			     48,000 bpd</p>
<p>  Olmeca exports			   501,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To North America		     501,000 bpd</p>
<p>Geographical Distribution</p>
<p>    North America			     82.3 pct</p>
<p>    Europe					14.4 pct</p>
<p>    Far East				     3.3 pct</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903. E-mail at timna.tanners@reuters.com))</p>
